# N: node N, a test node whose clock is 1500
N0 the Swift client listens as the sentinel -> listening 127.0.0.1:24702
N0 the node's join, edge store -> served sample n=3 store=tempus_edge sent=reply peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
N0 the node's join, bridge store -> served sample n=2 store=tempus_bridge sent=reply peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
N0 the node's join, sentinel store -> served sample n=2 store=tempus_sentinel sent=reply peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
N1 as the sentinel: sample tempus_sentinel 2 -> reply sample_reply entries=[0:9e1113ab416dc197] store=tempus_sentinel peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
N2 as an edge: sample tempus_edge 3 -> reply sample_reply entries=[1:9200d2990c3e9eb7] store=tempus_edge peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
N3 shuffle tempus_edge, its own entry at age 0 -> reply shuffle_reply entries=[1:9200d2990c3e9eb7] store=tempus_edge peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
N4 sample: the client is in the node's view at age 0 -> reply sample_reply entries=[1:9200d2990c3e9eb7,0:1fae2ad7f75a0ded] store=tempus_edge peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
N5 the Swift client listens as the edge -> listening 127.0.0.1:24703
N5 the trial tool sent node N 2 test-only ticks
N5 the node shuffles with the Swift client -> served shuffle entries=[0:b19edad2958934e1] store=tempus_edge sent=reply peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
N6 sample: the node took the entry the client answered with -> reply sample_reply entries=[4:12eb7f449478f2aa] store=tempus_edge peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
N7 an expired token -> closed at=challenge peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
N8 a token that is not valid yet -> closed at=challenge peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
N9 a token another key signed -> closed at=challenge peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
N10 a token under the old kid -> key_rotated at=challenge kid=6b31 peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
N11 a sample of more than the shuffle length -> closed at=reply peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
N12 a shuffle of the sentinel store that holds an edge's entry -> closed at=reply peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
N13 a call to a node that is not a bridge -> closed at=reply peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
N14 a cast to a node that is not a bridge -> closed at=reply peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
N15 the client's clock is past the node's token -> refused at=advert peer=b19edad2958934e1 reason="the token has expired"
N16 the client holds another producer kid and says so -> refused at=advert peer=b19edad2958934e1 reason="key_rotated"
N17 with a whitelist: an edge needs no entry in it -> reply sample_reply entries=[4:12eb7f449478f2aa] store=tempus_edge peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
N18 an address nobody listens on -> unreachable at=tls
# P: node P, which reads the system clock; the Swift client reads it too
# (P draws from the platform's random source: the entries of each reply are written here in sorted order)
P0 the Swift client listens as the sentinel -> listening 127.0.0.1:24704
P0 the node's join, edge store -> served sample n=3 store=tempus_edge sent=reply peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
P0 the node's join, bridge store -> served sample n=2 store=tempus_bridge sent=reply peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
P0 the node's join, sentinel store -> served sample n=2 store=tempus_sentinel sent=reply peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
P1 sample tempus_edge 3 -> reply sample_reply entries=[2:9200d2990c3e9eb7] store=tempus_edge peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
P2 shuffle tempus_edge, its own entry at age 0 -> reply shuffle_reply entries=[2:9200d2990c3e9eb7] store=tempus_edge peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
P3 sample: the client is in the node's view at age 0 -> reply sample_reply entries=[0:1fae2ad7f75a0ded,2:9200d2990c3e9eb7] store=tempus_edge peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
P4 the trial's token of 1000 to 3000 has expired by the system clock -> closed at=challenge peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
P5 a token that begins at 3900000000 is not valid yet -> closed at=challenge peer=b19edad2958934e1 typ=tempus_edge
# X1: the Swift client dials the Python example client
X1.1 a sample -> reply sample_reply entries=[3:9e1113ab416dc197] store=tempus_edge peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge
X1.2 a shuffle -> reply shuffle_reply entries=[1:9e1113ab416dc197] store=tempus_edge peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge
X1.3 a call -> reply result req_id=31 value=42 ver=1 peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge
X1.4 a cast, which has no reply -> closed at=reply peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge
X1.5 the peer presents somebody else's advert -> refused at=advert peer=9e1113ab416dc197 reason="the certificate's key is not the advert's pub"
X1.6 the peer's proof is over another nonce -> refused at=response peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge reason="the proof of possession does not verify"
X1.7 the peer's proof is by another key -> refused at=response peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge reason="the proof of possession does not verify"
X1.8 the peer's proof is 63 bytes -> refused at=response peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge reason="sig is not 64 bytes"
X1.9 the peer closes after its advert -> closed at=challenge peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge
X1.10 the peer sends a second advert where its challenge was due -> refused at=challenge peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge reason="advert where pop_challenge or key_rotated was due"
X1.11 a reply with an entry another key signed, beside a good one -> refused at=reply peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge reason="an entry does not verify: the signature does not verify"
X1.12 a reply of more entries than the shuffle length -> refused at=reply peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge reason="more entries than the shuffle length"
X1.13 a reply above the frame ceiling -> refused at=reply peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge reason="a frame above the ceiling"
X1.14 a reply that is no term -> refused at=reply peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge reason="bad_version"
X1.15 the peer closes instead of replying -> closed at=reply peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge
X1.16 the peer's token has expired -> refused at=advert peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 reason="the token has expired"
X1.17 the peer's token is under the old kid: the client says key_rotated -> refused at=advert peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 reason="key_rotated"
X1.18 the peer offers another ALPN protocol -> refused at=tls reason="the ALPN protocol is not tempus/1"
X1.19 the peer offers a P-256 certificate -> tls_failed at=tls
X1.20 the peer offers TLS 1.2 only -> tls_failed at=tls
# X2: the Python example client dials the Swift client
X2.0 the Swift client listens -> listening 127.0.0.1:24706
X2.1 a sample -> served sample n=2 store=tempus_edge sent=reply peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge
X2.2 a sample of 1 -> served sample n=1 store=tempus_edge sent=reply peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge
X2.3 a shuffle -> served shuffle entries=[0:e4188f0a2cee5a46] store=tempus_edge sent=reply peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge
X2.4 a sample of a store the client holds nothing for -> served sample n=2 store=tempus_bridge sent=reply peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge
X2.5 a test-only tick: to a client a frame of no kind, closed with no reply -> served tick store=tempus_edge sent=close peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge
X2.6 a call: a client is no bridge -> served call a=1 args=[1] f=f m=m opts={} req_id=31 ver=1 sent=close peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge
X2.7 somebody else's advert -> refused at=advert peer=9e1113ab416dc197 reason="the certificate's key is not the advert's pub"
X2.8 a proof by another key -> refused at=response peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge reason="the proof of possession does not verify"
X2.9 a proof over another nonce -> refused at=response peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge reason="the proof of possession does not verify"
X2.10 no proof: the request comes where it was due -> refused at=response peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge reason="sample where pop_response was due"
X2.11 the dialer closes instead of its proof -> closed at=response peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge
X2.12 a request above the frame ceiling -> refused at=request peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge reason="a frame above the ceiling"
X2.13 a request with an unknown key -> refused at=request peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge reason="unknown_field"
X2.14 a shuffle with an entry another key signed -> refused at=request peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge reason="an entry does not verify: the signature does not verify"
X2.15 a shuffle of the bridge store with an edge's entry -> refused at=request peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 typ=tempus_edge reason="an entry does not verify: the entry's typ is not the store's"
X2.16 an expired token -> refused at=advert peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 reason="the token has expired"
X2.17 a token under the old kid: the client says key_rotated -> refused at=advert peer=e4188f0a2cee5a46 reason="key_rotated"
X2.18 TLS 1.2 only -> tls_failed at=tls
X2.19 another ALPN protocol -> refused at=tls reason="the ALPN protocol is not tempus/1"
X2.20 no certificate -> tls_failed at=tls
X2.21 a P-256 certificate -> tls_failed at=tls
